DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     bbggppllggdd is a server which implements the FastCGI Protocol to execute
     bgpctl(8) commands.  bbggppllggdd is a simple server that implements a simple
     web API to query bgpd(8).

     bbggppllggdd opens a socket at _/_v_a_r_/_w_w_w_/_r_u_n_/_b_g_p_l_g_d_._s_o_c_k, owned by www:www, with
     permissions 0660.  It will then drop privileges to user "_bgplgd",
     unveil(2) the bgpctl(8) binary and restrict itself with pledge(2).

     The options are as follows:

     --dd      Do not daemonize.  If this option is specified, bbggppllggdd will run
             in the foreground and log to stderr.

     --pp _p_a_t_h
             Use _p_a_t_h instead of bgpctl(8) to query bgpd(8).

     --SS _s_o_c_k_e_t
             Use _s_o_c_k_e_t instead of the default _/_v_a_r_/_r_u_n_/_b_g_p_d_._r_s_o_c_k to communi‐
             cate with bgpd(8).

     --ss _s_o_c_k_e_t
             Create and bind to alternative local socket at _s_o_c_k_e_t.

     --UU _u_s_e_r
             Change the owner of _/_v_a_r_/_w_w_w_/_r_u_n_/_b_g_p_l_g_d_._s_o_c_k to _u_s_e_r and its pri‐
             mary group instead of the default www:www.

     --VV      Show the version and exit.

     bbggppllggdd provides the following API endpoints.  Unless further specified
     the endpoints do not take any parameters:

     _/_i_n_t_e_r_f_a_c_e_s  Show the interface states.
     _/_m_e_m_o_r_y      Show RIB memory statistics.
     _/_m_e_t_r_i_c_s     Output various statistics in OpenMetrics format.
     _/_n_e_i_g_h_b_o_r_s   Show detailed neighbors information.  The output can be lim‐
                  ited with the following parameters:

                  nneeiigghhbboorr=_p_e_e_r  Show information for a specific neighbor.
                                 _p_e_e_r may be the neighbor's address or de‐
                                 scription.
                  ggrroouupp=_n_a_m_e     Show only entries from the specified peer
                                 group.
     _/_n_e_x_t_h_o_p_s    Show the list of BGP nexthops and the result of their valid‐
                  ity check.
     _/_r_i_b
     _/_r_i_b_/_i_n
     _/_r_i_b_/_o_u_t     Show routes from the bgpd(8) Routing Information Base.  For
                  _/_r_i_b_/_i_n the _A_d_j_-_R_I_B_-_I_n will be queried and for _/_r_i_b_/_o_u_t the
                  _A_d_j_-_R_I_B_-_o_u_t.  The following parameters can be used to filter
                  the output:

                  nneeiigghhbboorr=_p_e_e_r  Show information for a specific neighbor.
                                 _p_e_e_r may be the neighbor's address or de‐
                                 scription.
                  ggrroouupp=_n_a_m_e     Show only entries from the specified peer
                                 group.
                  aass=_n_u_m_b_e_r      Show only entries with the specified source
                                 AS number.
                  ccoommmmuunniittyy=_s_t_r_i_n_g
                  eexxtt--ccoommmmuunniittyy=_s_t_r_i_n_g
                  llaarrggee--ccoommmmuunniittyy=_s_t_r_i_n_g
                                 Show only entries that match the specified
                                 community.
                  aaff=(iippvv44 | iippvv66 | vvppnnvv44 | vvppnnvv66)
                                 Show only entries that match the specified
                                 address family.
                  rriibb=_n_a_m_e       Show only entries from the RIB with name
                                 _n_a_m_e.  Can only be used with the _/_r_i_b end‐
                                 point.
                  oovvss=(vvaalliidd | nnoott--ffoouunndd | iinnvvaalliidd)
                                 Show only prefixes that match the specified
